    {
      "id": "rn_NPzyvfByCy3bwH6f::L2::Q8",
      "moduleId": "rn_NPzyvfByCy3bwH6f::L2",
      "stem": "Explain why the cell wall and the cell membrane are NOT interchangeable in a labelled diagram.",
      "misconceptionClass": "wall vs membrane",
      "kind": "explain-why",
      "modelAnswer": "The wall is the rigid cellulose outer layer giving shape and protection, while the membrane is the thin selective barrier controlling traffic; one is structural scaffolding, the other the gatekeeper, so a diagram that labels one where the other belongs misstates the cell's design.",
